    "updated_at": "2021-06-04T04:51:08Z",
    "body": "I think it's fine to use for all cases where you have a byte sequence and want to return it isomomorphic decoded for convenience.  It's typically network APIs that need this as they never adopted Unicode.\r\n\r\nE.g., I think https://w3c.github.io/resource-timing/#dom-performanceresourcetiming-nexthopprotocol should use it too. (Tracked in https://github.com/w3c/resource-timing/issues/274.)",
